## 7. COMPLEXITY ANALYSIS LAB

Add an interactive complexity analysis workspace.

Features:

- Analyze loops and nested loops.
- Explain logarithmic loops.
- Explain recursive algorithms.
- Generate recurrence relations.
- Solve supported recurrences step by step.
- Compare asymptotic growth rates.
- Plot growth curves.
- Compare algorithm performance as input size increases.
- Explain dominant terms.
- Show why constants and lower-order terms are omitted asymptotically.
- Demonstrate best, average, and worst cases.
- Compare theoretical complexity with measured execution time when benchmarking is available.

Include growth classes such as:

O(1), O(log n), O(n), O(n log n), O(n²), O(n³), O(2ⁿ), and O(n!).

Clearly distinguish theoretical complexity from measured runtime. Do not infer complexity solely from one runtime measurement.

